WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.433
In today's Cloud Minute I'll show you how to create a postgres instance via Cloud Launcher.

00:00:03.433 --> 00:00:06.166
Starting on the Cloud Launcher homepage click database

00:00:10.366 --> 00:00:11.800
and then click PostgreSQL

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:15.900
Click launch on Google Cloud Platform 

00:00:16.866 --> 00:00:17.900
Pick the project where you'd like

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:21.100
the Postgres instance to be created and then click the continue button

00:00:23.866 --> 00:00:25.900
It may take a couple minutes for the next screen to appear.

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:28.666
You will see a progress bar indicating that it is initializing.

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:32.833
Give the VM a name and configure it in a way that makes sense for your project.

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:41.766
Again launching the instance may take a couple minutes.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.766
Note the username and password.

00:00:44.866 --> 00:00:48.033
Click SSH to login to the machine using the in browser terminal.

00:00:48.966 --> 00:00:50.900
Now your postgres instance is created.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:56.466
Please check out our other cloud minutes.

